00:38:21,681 --> 00:38:27,420
perhaps the world's most famous restaurant, La Tour d'Argent, located on the right bank

492
00:38:27,421 --> 00:38:30,273
of Paris in the shadow of Notre Dame.

493
00:38:30,274 --> 00:38:34,360
Founded in 1582, La Tour was a favorite meeting place

494
00:38:34,361 --> 00:38:39,252
of King Henry III, who often stopped by after hunting along the Seine.

495
00:38:39,253 --> 00:38:40,440
Legend holds that

496
00:38:40,441 --> 00:38:43,372
it was here that he learned to eat with a fork.

497
00:38:43,373 --> 00:38:45,680
Since then, the restaurant has served

498
00:38:45,681 --> 00:38:51,320
the rich and powerful for centuries. Not surprisingly, 30 feet below the restaurant

499
00:38:51,321 --> 00:38:54,765
itself is perhaps the world's finest wine cellar.

500
00:38:54,766 --> 00:38:58,420
One that dates back to the 1820s when the restaurant

501
00:38:58,421 --> 00:39:03,685
was rebuilt after being burned during the French Revolution.

502
00:39:03,686 --> 00:39:07,020
The oldest wine bottle is an 1845 now.

503
00:39:07,220 --> 00:39:11,881
Unfortunately the 1811 comet year from Lafitte got broken by one of my cellarmen.

504
00:39:11,882 --> 00:39:13,320
We had to get rid of him.

505
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:20,200
Currently the cellar holds upwards of 450,000 bottles, including all of the most prized

506
00:39:20,201 --> 00:39:21,900
vintages in French wine history.

507
00:39:23,660 --> 00:39:25,820
1968 Gros-Laroze.

508
00:39:26,500 --> 00:39:28,120
Gros-Laroze is Saint-Julien,

509
00:39:28,320 --> 00:39:29,640
Cabernet-based wine.

510
00:39:30,280 --> 00:39:32,060
And that is, like, amazing

511
00:39:32,061 --> 00:39:33,000
to imagine that

512
00:39:33,001 --> 00:39:35,960
still with us.

513
00:39:38,600 --> 00:39:40,060
The cellar's temperature

514
00:39:40,061 --> 00:39:42,120
naturally ranges no higher or lower

515
00:39:42,121 --> 00:39:44,380
than 53 to 59 degrees,

516
00:39:44,840 --> 00:39:46,100
while the humidity stays

517
00:39:46,101 --> 00:39:48,340
