518
00:39:48,341 --> 00:39:49,940
It's considered the most

519
00:39:49,941 --> 00:39:56,220
technically perfect cellar in the City of Lights.

520
00:39:56,221 --> 00:40:00,240
Aging is one of wine's greatest traditions. Yet even today,

521
00:40:00,241 --> 00:40:05,380
no one knows exactly what happens to wine as it transforms over time.

522
00:40:05,381 --> 00:40:08,460
Some have theorized that chemical elements within the wine,

523
00:40:08,461 --> 00:40:12,480
primarily the tannins, bond with other compounds.

524
00:40:12,481 --> 00:40:17,260
Others suggest those same compounds are broken down.

525
00:40:17,261 --> 00:40:22,140
What's clear is that the aromas and flavors become more numerous, layered, and sophisticated.

526
00:40:22,800 --> 00:40:26,560
Two days ago, we had a bottle of Vinay-Claude Duchesne, 1885.

